---
title: "calculate_liquidation_amounts (Scallop Sui Lending Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_max_repay: max_repay = max_repay_amount(obligation, market, ...)
    q_max_repay --> q_actual_repay: actual_repay = min(available_repay_amount, max_repay)
    q_actual_repay --> q_check_repay: actual_repay > 0
    q_check_repay --> q_convert: actual_repay > 0
    q_check_repay --> q_abort_zero: actual_repay == 0
    q_abort_zero --> [*]: abort unable_to_liquidate_error
    q_convert --> q_check_collateral: (liq_amount, protocol_amount) = debt_to_collateral_amount(actual_repay)
    q_check_collateral --> q_scale: total_needed > total_collateral
    q_check_collateral --> q_no_scale: total_needed <= total_collateral
    q_scale --> q_scaled_result: proportionally scale (actual_repay, liq_amount, protocol_amount)
    q_no_scale --> q_check_final: (actual_repay, liq_amount, protocol_amount)
    q_scaled_result --> q_check_final: scaled values
    q_check_final --> [*]: return (actual_repay, liq_amount, protocol_amount)

    note right of q_max_repay
        INV-001: max_repay capped at 20% of total debt value (LIQUIDATION_CAP_DIVISOR=5)
        INV-002: dust positions (total_debt <= $10) bypass 20% cap for full clearance
    end note

    note right of q_convert
        INV-003: exchange_rate = (collateral_scale/debt_scale) * (debt_price/collateral_price)
        INV-004: liq_amount = actual_repay * exchange_rate * (1 + liq_discount)
        INV-005: protocol_amount = actual_repay * exchange_rate * liq_revenue_factor
    end note

    note right of q_scale
        INV-006: when collateral insufficient, all three values scaled by same ratio
        INV-007: scaling ratio = total_collateral / (liq_amount + protocol_amount)
        INV-008: prevents liquidator from paying more than collateral received
    end note
